TIP:  For the intro, place your index finger on the top string/2nd fret.  Now pick the top string, cover the top string next to it on the 3rd fret with your middle finger and pick, lift off and pick the open 5th string on your way to forming the (D).

TIP:  The (A) (A7) (A), (A) - (A) - (A) - (D) appears in the intro and at the end of the verse and is kind of important, but is easy to play if you remember what you're trying to achieve.  It's a walk-down voicing with each chord emphasizing a particular string.  The first (A) and the (A7) is the 3rd string, but that third (A) is the 4th string that's the one you need to hit.  The next three (A)s are strummed together and emphasize the 5th striing.  Even the ending (D) focuses on the 4th string.  So during the whole thing aim for the middle strings and kind of "stab" your way from the 3rd to the 5th strings.
       
TIP:  (Gm) isn't played too often but it's just like the (Fm) or (F#m) but played on the 3rd fret.  


